From 381d1fbc0f2a4205926ea99bba2a984bd95d5b24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mercury-3 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:25:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(providers): per-user rate limit for outbound
 probe/discovery routes

Add a dedicated per-user TokenBucket (default 20/min, tunable via
SWARM_PROVIDER_PROBE_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN) for provider test and model-discovery
routes, mirroring lensBucket. POST /api/providers/test, /discover, and
/[id]/test now consume one token per request right before the outbound call
and return 429 with Retry-After when a user's budget is exhausted, so
outbound DNS/HTTP bursts are bounded per account instead of sharing only the
app-wide bucket.

Tests: rapid probe calls from one user are throttled (429) while another
user is unaffected, on all three routes.

Gates: typecheck 0 errors; unit 2568 pass / 0 fail / 1 skipped; build exit 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
